>
  <section id="scope">
    <h2>What this Champion guide covers</h2>
    <p>This is an independent buyer-research page about Champion residential standby systems. It is not a Champion sales page, dealer page, field-reliability study, or hands-on product test. We use Champion’s own current product pages, manuals, warranty material, and installation guidance for Champion-specific facts, then separate those facts from buyer questions and unknowns.</p>
    <p>Champion’s current home-standby catalog contains multiple generator/ATS packages. The important unit of comparison is therefore the <strong>exact package model</strong>, selected fuel, transfer-switch rating, load-management plan, and site-specific installation scope—not simply the Champion brand name or a headline kW number.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="current-models">
    <h2>Current Champion model families a homeowner is likely to encounter</h2>
    <p>Champion’s current catalog includes 26 kW fleX systems, 22 kW fleX systems, 22 kW aXis systems, and additional lower-output/select-circuit products. The catalog also varies the included transfer-switch amperage across packages. That means two “Champion 22 kW” or “Champion 26 kW” quotes may not contain the same switch or control architecture.</p>
    <div class="not-prose mt-5 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-[#d9e0ea]">
      <table class="mobile-card-table sm:min-w-[860px] w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm">
        <caption class="sr-only">Examples of current Champion home standby package families</caption>
        <thead class="bg-[#edf3fb] text-primary">
          <tr><th class="p-3">Example package</th><th class="p-3">Published output</th><th class="p-3">Included transfer equipment</th><th class="p-3">Buyer note</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200 text-gray-800">
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" class="p-3">201614 · 26 kW fleX</th>
